1
00:00:00,406 --> 00:00:02,446
Leonard, you're my friend...

2
00:00:02,617 --> 00:00:05,497
(Sheldon:)...and friends support their friends,
apparently.

3
00:00:06,079 --> 00:00:07,709
(Sheldon:)So I am withdrawing my objection...

4
00:00:07,872 --> 00:00:11,332
(Sheldon:)...to your desire
to have a relationship with Leslie.

5
00:00:11,501 --> 00:00:14,041
- Thank you.
- I will graciously overlook the fact...

6
00:00:14,212 --> 00:00:16,632
(Sheldon:)...that she is an arrogant,
subpar scientist...

7
00:00:16,798 --> 00:00:20,088
...who believes loop quantum gravity
better unites quantum mechanics...

8
00:00:20,259 --> 00:00:23,679
(Sheldon:)...with general relativity
than does string theory.

9
00:00:24,305 --> 00:00:26,345
(Sheldon:)You kids have fun.

10
00:00:26,516 --> 00:00:28,146
(Leslie:)Hang on a second.

11
00:00:28,309 --> 00:00:32,059
(Leslie:)Loop quantum gravity clearly offers more
testable predictions than string theory.

12
00:00:32,563 --> 00:00:35,523
(Sheldon:)I'm listening. Amuse me.

13
00:00:35,691 --> 00:00:38,441
(Leslie:)Okay, well, for one thing,
we expect quantized space-time...

14
00:00:38,611 --> 00:00:42,361
...to manifest as minute differences
in the speed of light for different colors.

15
00:00:42,532 --> 00:00:46,572
(Sheldon:)Balderdash.
Matter clearly consists of tiny strings.

16
00:00:47,954 --> 00:00:50,544
Are you gonna let him talk to me
like that?

17
00:00:55,211 --> 00:00:57,631
(Penny:)Okay, well,
there is a lot of merit to both theories.

18
00:00:57,797 --> 00:01:01,717
(Leslie:)No, there isn't. Only loop quantum gravity
calculates the entropy of black holes.

